# React / Next.js Rules

## Component Design
- Functional components only — no class components
- Single responsibility: one component does one thing
- Custom hooks for all business logic — never in component body
- Props interfaces explicitly typed — never use 'any'

## State Management
- Local state: useState for UI-only state
- Server state: TanStack Query (React Query) for API data
- Global state: Zustand for cross-component state
- Never use Redux — overkill for this project

## Real-Time (WebSocket)
- Socket.io client for all real-time ping/call feed
- Auto-reconnect with exponential backoff
- Scoped to tenant room only — never global broadcast
- Show connection status to user always

## Performance
- Code split all heavy components (charts, flow builder) — lazy load
- React.memo for expensive list items
- useMemo/useCallback only when profiler shows regression
- Bundle size target: under 200KB gzipped initial load

## Styling
- Tailwind CSS only — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- No fixed pixel widths — responsive from mobile up

## Error Handling
- Error boundaries on all major sections
- Suspense boundaries for all async components
- Never let uncaught errors crash the entire dashboard